  "properties": {
    "title": "Land Use Land Cover (NRSC): 2017 - 2018",
    "description": "Annual Land Use Land Cover maps for India built by National Remote Sensing Center, Indian Space Research Organization (ISRO) and available on India Water Resources Information System (WRIS) [portal](https://indiawris.gov.in/wris/#/).\n\nThe annual maps are available from 2005 onwards at 56m resolution.\n \nFollowing classes exist in the map: \n1. Built Up\n2. Cropland -  Kharif\n3. Cropland - Rabi\n4. Cropland - Zaid\n5. Cropland - Double/Triple\n6. Fallow Land - Current Fallow\n7. Agriculture Plantation - Plantation\n8. Forest - Evergreen/Semi-Evergreen\n9. Forest - Deciduous\n10. Forest - Degraded/Scrub\n11. Forest - Littoral Swamp\n12. Natural - Grassland\n13. Other - Shifting Cultivation\n14. Wasteland\n15. Sandy Area - Rann\n16. Waterbodies - Max\n17. Waterbodies - Min\n18. Snow Covered / Glacial Area   \n",
